  "description": "the parallel-plate cell through m.chem_mesh(): CurrentDistribution of order 2, primary electrodes (E_eq = 0) at phi_s = dV on anode (x = 0) and 0 on cathode (x = gap), the other boundary insulating, kappa by element attribute; phi = dV (1 - x/gap) is exact in P2, and the electrode current per metre, kappa grad phi . n over the electrode (n outward, anodic positive), is I = kappa dV Hc / gap on the anode and -I on the cathode",
  "build": "any",
  "mesh": "the mesher's unstructured mesh of the document (gmsh, bounded planar mode, algorithm and options of axmp-mesher), mesh.size = gap/16, geometry order 2 (the default: straight edges, with nodes; the exporter lists no edge node); one process",
  "instance": null,
  "solver": {
    "order": 2,
